# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_branch_delete_lane_release.py" "BRANCH DELETE LANE RELEASE GATE: PASS" "branch delete releases stale BR lanes" "branch delete releases stale BR lanes: a non-main branch push reserves lanes under BR-branch before any PR exists; when GitHub sends the branch-delete push, Veripsa releases that BR change immediately so later PRs do not wait behind a deleted remote branch. The gate drives the real make_db_processor against scratch Postgres, proves push reserve, delete release, no phantom contention for a later PR on the same file, and same-branch re-push still works. Content-free: branch refs, repo ids, paths, and claim counts only; no source or diff bodies." "branch-delete push releases BR-branch lanes immediately and prevents ghost in-flight contention from deleted remote branches" 18
